### Variables (reuse from payment-intents.http if already defined there)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@paymentIntentId = 35ae69a3-2baa-40de-b33c-68ad06c9d1e2

### 0. Login to get token (run this first, or whenever token expires)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 1. Create a refund (happy path)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-001
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 500
}

### 2. Replay the same request (same Idempotency-Key) — should return identical response, no new row
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-001
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 500
}

### 3. Second partial refund with a NEW idempotency key — should succeed if within remaining balance
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-002
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 400
}

### 4. Over-balance refund — should return 409 with remainingBalance + requestAmount populated
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-003
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 999999
}

### 5. Missing Idempotency-Key header — should return 400 (MissingRequestHeaderException)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1000
}

### 6. Invalid amount (fails @Min(1) / @NotNull validation) — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-004
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": -5
}

### 7. Nonexistent payment intent — should return 404 via PaymentIntentNotFoundException
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-key-005
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1000
}

### ============================================
### Ownership tests — cross-merchant access
### ============================================

### 8. Login as a SECOND, different merchant
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "merchant-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("otherMerchantToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 9. OTHER merchant tries to refund merchant A's SUCCEEDED payment intent
# Use a paymentIntentId that belongs to the FIRST merchant (SUCCEEDED status, from payment-intents.http request 8).
# Expect: 404 Not Found — ownership check should hide existence, not leak a 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-ownership-test-001
Authorization: Bearer {{otherMerchantToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 100
}